p_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02715741191878603,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":41.3,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02204091379447584,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":63.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.08282,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":55.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"FTAI Infrastructure Inc. engages in acquiring, developing, and operating assets and businesses that represent infrastructure for customers in the transportation, energy, and industrial products industries in North America. It operates through four segments: Railroad, Ports and Terminals, Power and Gas, and Sustainability and Energy Transition. The company operates a multi-modal crude oil and refined products terminal, and other related assets; and Jefferson Terminal and Repauno that develops or acquires industrial properties in strategic locations that store and handle for third parties various energy products, including crude oil, refined products, and clean fuels. It also has a 1,630-acre deep-water port located along the Delaware River with an underground storage cavern, a multipurpose dock, a rail-to-ship transloading system, and multiple industrial development opportunities; and a 1,660-acre multi-modal port located along the Ohio River with rail, dock, and multiple industrial development opportunities, including a power plant. In addition, the company owns and operates eight freight railroads and one switching company that provides rail service to certain manufacturing and production facilities. Further, it focuses on waste plastic to renewable fuel, hydrogen-fueled power plant, and carbon capture businesses. FTAI Infrastructure Inc. was incorporated in 2021 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kenneth J. Nicholson | CEO & President | Age 54","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $453K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 24%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["FTAI Infrastructure Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $410M market cap on $503M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +24% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -10% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $399M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 8.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (26.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 40% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"FTAI Infrastructure (FIP) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/ftai-infrastructure-fip-q3-2026-183209000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793990616.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Ftai Infrastructure forecasts continued double-digit rail growth as Long Ridge sale targets end-of-month close (NASDAQ:FIP)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668384-ftai-infrastructure-forecasts-continued-double-digit-rail-growth-as-long-ridge-sale-targets","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793986644.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.637,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"FTAI Infrastructure (NASDAQ:FIP) Announces Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/ftai-infrastructure-nasdaqfip-announces-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793981718.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"FIP Q3 2026 deep dive: rail growth, asset sales, and terminal transformation shape outlook","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https: